    "description": [
     "\"A Dutton book.\"",
     "Flirting with the dark angel -- Indians and buffalo grass -- A sort of Tom Sawyer -- \"$2 and a clean shirt\" -- The lieutenant takes a bride -- First five-and-dime days -- \"$60,000--and no more!\" -- An aristocratic country town -- Airplanes and hula hoops -- \"A hell of an idea!\" -- Watermelons and a donkey mess -- Finding a few key men -- The courtship of Ron Mayer -- \"I need money--quick!\" -- Stylus virum arguit -- To crown a new king -- Inside the family circle -- New chiefs and computers -- Guinea pig--or death? -- Wholesale and hometown -- Corporate shake-up -- Labor unions not welcome -- The nine-billion-dollar man -- The war over Main Street -- Clerks and customers -- \"Oh, it's a big sky\" -- And the race goes on ... -- Epilogue",
     "Presents the rags-to-riches tale of billionaire Sam Walton, founder of the discount chain Wal-Mart and America's richest man, as a study in old-fashioned values such as honesty and hard work"
    ],
